The central bankers are going in,

00:48:06.340 --> 00:48:09.100
taking their resources and then putting them in debt.

00:48:09.300 --> 00:48:11.380
So it's a different philosophy.

00:48:11.580 --> 00:48:15.340
And they're going to have more power than us by doing it like that.

00:48:15.540 --> 00:48:15.940
Yes.

00:48:16.140 --> 00:48:17.380
No, they're not they're not done.

00:48:17.580 --> 00:48:19.100
Oh, no. And they're very patient.

00:48:19.300 --> 00:48:21.700
They have a long term view and we don't.

00:48:21.900 --> 00:48:23.500
We have a short to medium term view.

00:48:23.700 --> 00:48:26.180
You know, in 2008, the the Greek government,

00:48:26.420 --> 00:48:30.460
the Greek economy, rather collapsed, like literally collapsed.

00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:31.660
And it was their own fault.

00:48:31.860 --> 00:48:34.860
It was years and years and years of just wasting money.

00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:39.980
And so the World Bank, the International Monetary Fund and the European Central

00:48:40.180 --> 00:48:43.140
Bank went in and said, OK, here's what you're going to do.

00:48:43.140 --> 00:48:44.300
We're going to give you these giant

00:48:44.500 --> 00:48:48.500
loans and then you're going to be essentially our prisoner.

00:48:48.700 --> 00:48:54.420
And so they did at first, they accepted these onerous terms.

00:48:54.620 --> 00:49:00.380
They ended up missing a payment to the IMF and then the IMF withdrew.

00:49:00.580 --> 00:49:04.060
And so the Greeks, rather than to be angry

00:49:04.060 --> 00:49:06.900
at their own government for wasting money for so many years,

00:49:07.100 --> 00:49:11.660
they were angry at the World Bank, the IMF and the European Central Bank.

00:49:11.860 --> 00:49:16.300
But then the Chinese stepped in and said, listen, you guys need money.

00:49:16.500 --> 00:49:17.860
We have lots of money.

00:49:18.060 --> 00:49:20.940
So how about if we buy the Port of Piraeus,

00:49:21.140 --> 00:49:24.980
which is the largest cargo port in the world,

00:49:25.180 --> 00:49:32.780
we'll buy the Port of Thessaloniki and the Port of Hanya in Crete and we'll pay cash.

00:49:32.980 --> 00:49:34.260
And so they did.

